{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["מעקה — it has no cognate in the Torah; it is like the form of מַעֲשֶׂה, מַרְאֶה. But עקת רשע, תעיק העגלה, מעיק תחתיכם — these are from the root ע-ק-ק."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "Rashbam contrasts מעקה (from ע-ק-ה, like מַעֲשֶׂה/מַרְאֶה with middle letter dropped) against forms from the root ע-ק-ק; I rendered the latter group's shared root explicitly to clarify the grammatical point for the English reader."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:39:20.211820869Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}